            <ArticleTitle>Congenital posterior atlas defect associated with anterior rachischisis and early cervical degenerative disc disease: a case study and review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>282-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A rare case of a wide congenital atlas defect is reported. A 25 year-old woman was admitted after complaints of radicular pain in the right arm. Radiographs incidentally revealed aplasia of the posterior arch of the atlas together with anterior rachischisis. A review of the literature is presented and a possible association with early disc degeneration is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
